00:06:11.216 --> 00:06:20.144
<v Host>Hayabusa2 succeeded in gathering observation data with all four of its instruments, including cameras and infrared devices.

00:06:20.744 --> 00:06:23.120
<v Vocab>観測

00:06:23.519 --> 00:06:28.175
<v Host>It means observation — watching and measuring something scientifically.

00:06:28.776 --> 00:06:42.024
<v Slow>今回の成功で、日本は数百メートルほどの小惑星に、探査機を正確に近づける技術を証明しました。

00:06:42.824 --> 00:06:51.079
<v Host>With this success, Japan proved it can bring a probe precisely close to an asteroid just a few hundred meters across.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.031
<v Vocab>証明

00:06:54.432 --> 00:06:57.456
<v Host>It means proof, or to prove something.

00:06:58.055 --> 00:07:12.576
<v Slow>この技術は、将来、地球に近づく危険な小惑星の進む道を変える「地球防衛」に役立つと期待されています。

00:07:13.375 --> 00:07:21.560
<v Host>This technology is expected to help with planetary defense — changing the path of a dangerous asteroid heading toward Earth.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:24.536
<v Vocab>防衛

00:07:24.935 --> 00:07:28.271
<v Host>It means defense, protecting against something.

00:07:28.872 --> 00:07:42.072
<v Slow>はやぶさ2は、2020年に小惑星「リュウグウ」の砂を地球に届けたあと、新しいミッションを続けています。

00:07:42.872 --> 00:07:51.223
<v Host>After delivering sand from the asteroid Ryugu to Earth in twenty twenty, Hayabusa2 has continued on a new mission.

00:07:51.824 --> 00:07:54.199
<v Vocab>届ける

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:58.295
<v Host>It means to deliver, to bring something to its destination.

