00:11:42.152 --> 00:12:15.224
<v Host>That's all for today. On July fifth, Japan's probe Hayabusa2 made a super-close, high-speed flyby of the asteroid Torifune, about seven million kilometers from Earth. It came within roughly eight hundred meters of the asteroid's center at about five kilometers per second, and all four of its instruments collected data. The success shows Japan can steer a probe precisely up to a small asteroid — a skill that could one day help protect Earth. Thanks for listening, and see you tomorrow.

00:12:15.823 --> 00:12:18.224
